# Isolated live database

`mars_local` remains the synthetic development database. Do not relabel it as
live, do not mix real records into it, and do not delete it without explicit
authorisation.

When real DHIS2 metadata or later patient synchronisation is approved, use a
**separate** PostgreSQL database named `mars_live`.

Copy this file to a secret-managed environment, never into the repository as a
filled `.env`.

```
MARS_ENVIRONMENT=local
MARS_DEMO_MODE_ENABLED=false
MARS_DEV_AUTH_ENABLED=false
MARS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://mars_live_user@127.0.0.1:5432/mars_live
MARS_DHIS2_ENABLED=false
MARS_DHIS2_PUSH_ENABLED=false
MARS_DHIS2_DISCOVERY_BASE_URL=https://eregisters.health.go.ug
# Token: session environment only. Never this file, a URL, a log or a report.
# MARS_DHIS2_DISCOVERY_TOKEN=
```

Rules:

- Demo mode stays off.
- No synthetic seeder against `mars_live`.
- DHIS2 credentials stay server-side.
- Upstream writes stay disabled (`MARS_DHIS2_PUSH_ENABLED=false`).
- A Pader-scoped account must produce a Pader Overview, never a national one.
- Do not claim the dashboard is live until a bounded source synchronisation has
  completed successfully.
